; Interprets: 3GPP TS 29.128
;; What TS 29.128's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order: the procedures' information-element tables (clause 5),
;; the protocol's common aspects (clause 6.1), the result codes (6.3) and the
;; AVPs (6.4). Each command is printed once under 16777346, for T6a/T6b,
;; T6ai/T6bi and T7 alike, so a table describing one direction of a command
;; (the MME's CMR of clause 5.7.1, the SCEF's of 5.8.1) describes the one
;; print. A rule depending on a node, a feature, the subscription or an
;; earlier message is `text-only`.


;; Clause 5.2.1's tables. What the request is sent for it does not carry.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-monitoring-event-report
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.1
; Table: 5.2.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"If the Reporting-Information-Request is sent for reporting the monitoring events, the MME/SGSN and the IWK-SCEF shall include the monitoring event(s) reported towards the SCEF."
    text-only


;; Each answer's Result row: the T6a/b errors are 3GPP's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ria-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.2.1
; Table: 5.2.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for T6a/b errors. This is a grouped AVP, which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Clause 5.2.2, the report's contents, read on the RIR through paths into
;; its Monitoring-Event-Reports (the configuration answer's immediate report
;; is clause 5.3.1's); the body requires SCEF-Reference-ID itself.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-monitoring-event-report-identities
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.2.0
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"For all monitoring events, the SCEF-ID, the SCEF-Reference-ID/SCEF-Reference-ID-Ext and the Monitoring-Type AVPs shall be included."
    requires Monitoring-Event-Report/SCEF-ID and Monitoring-Event-Report/Monitoring-Type


;; The subscription.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-user-identifier
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 5.2.2.0
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The MME/SGSN shall include the External-Identifier or the MSISDN if present in the subscription data received from the HSS."
    text-only


;; The event a report carries is its Monitoring-Type, TS 29.336's Unsigned32,
;; whose values the corpus does not read, written as numbers; with 8 the
;; NOTE tells a reachability report from an idle status one.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reachability-information-event
; AVP: Reachability-Information
; Within: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Section: 5.2.2.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The following AVPs shall be present within the Monitoring-Event-Report AVP when the UE Reachability event is reported:"
"- Monitoring-Type set to either UE_REACHABILITY (1) or UE_REACHABILITY_AND_IDLE_STATUS_INDICATION (8), as received in the configuration request."
"- Reachability-Information set to REACHABLE_FOR_DATA(1)"
"NOTE: When the Monitoring-Type is UE_REACHABILITY_AND_IDLE_STATUS_INDICATION (8), absence of the Idle-Status-Indication AVP from the Monitoring-Event-Report AVP indicates that UE reachability is reported."
    present-if Monitoring-Type = 1 or Monitoring-Type = 8 and not Idle-Status-Indication
    values 1 if Monitoring-Type = 1 or Monitoring-Type = 8 and not Idle-Status-Indication


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: eps-location-information-event
; AVP: EPS-Location-Information
; Within: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Section: 5.2.2.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The following AVPs shall be present within the Monitoring-Event-Report AVP when the location event is reported:"
"- Monitoring-Type set to LOCATION_REPORTING (2)"
"- EPS-Location-Information"
    present-if Monitoring-Type = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: communication-failure-information-event
; AVP: Communication-Failure-Information
; Within: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Section: 5.2.2.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The following AVPs shall be present within the Monitoring-Event-Report AVP when the Communication Failure event is reported"
"- Monitoring-Type set to COMMUNICATION_FAILURE (5)"
"- Communication-Failure-Information (see clause 6.4.3)"
    present-if Monitoring-Type = 5


;; The clause numbers PDN_CONNECTIVITY_STATUS 8, UE_REACHABILITY_AND_IDLE_
;; STATUS_INDICATION's value (clause 5.2.2.2); TS 29.336 clause 8.4.7 numbers
;; it 10: which value the rule reads the document does not settle.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pdn-connectivity-status-report-event
; AVP: PDN-Connectivity-Status-Report
; Within: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Section: 5.2.2.7
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"- Monitoring-Type set to PDN_CONNECTIVITY_STATUS (8)"
"- PDN-Connectivity-Status-Report"
    text-only


;; As clause 5.2.2.7's: 9 is AVAILABILITY_AFTER_DDN_FAILURE_AND_IDLE_STATUS_
;; INDICATION's, and TS 29.336 numbers SAT_SF_OPERATION_INFO 11.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sat-sf-operation-info-event
; AVP: SAT-SF-Operation-Info
; Within: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Section: 5.2.2.8
; Versions: 19.2.0
"- Monitoring-Type set to SAT_SF_OPERATION_INFO (9)"
"- SAT-SF-Operation-Info"
    text-only


;; Clause 5.3.1's tables. Whether a report is available the answer does not
;; show.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-monitoring-event-report
; AVP: Monitoring-Event-Report
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.3.1
; Table: 5.3.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"If an immediate report is available this information element shall contain the requested data available in the MME/SGSN."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-5-3-1-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.3.1
; Table: 5.3.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for T6a/T6b errors. This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Clause 5.4.1's tables, the CIR the MME/SGSN sends the IWK-SCEF.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cia-5-4-1-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Configuration-Information-Answer
; Section: 5.4.1
; Table: 5.4.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for T6a/b errors. This is a grouped AVP which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Clause 5.5.1's tables. TS 29.336's grouped AVP carries the IMSI in its
;; User-Name, read through a path from the command.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: odr-user-identifier-imsi
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: MO-Data-Request
; Section: 5.5.1
; Table: 5.5.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present and shall contain the identity of the UE. This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the IMSI."
    requires User-Identifier/User-Name


;; Whether the request conveys data is the AVP's presence: no rule a
;; message can break.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: odr-non-ip-data
; AVP: Non-IP-Data
; Command: MO-Data-Request
; Section: 5.5.1
; Table: 5.5.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present when the request conveys Non-IP data."
    text-only


;; What the MME needs to send.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: odr-rrc-cause-counter
; AVP: RRC-Cause-Counter
; Command: MO-Data-Request
; Section: 5.5.1
; Table: 5.5.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The MME shall include this Information Element when MME needs to send a non-zero counter value for the MO Exception Data Counter."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: oda-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: MO-Data-Answer
; Section: 5.5.1
; Table: 5.5.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for T6a/b errors. This is a grouped AVP, which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Clause 5.6.1's tables.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tdr-user-identifier-imsi
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: MT-Data-Request
; Section: 5.6.1
; Table: 5.6.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present and shall contain the identity of the UE. This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the IMSI."
    requires User-Identifier/User-Name


;; As the ODR's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tdr-non-ip-data
; AVP: Non-IP-Data
; Command: MT-Data-Request
; Section: 5.6.1
; Table: 5.6.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present when the request conveys Non-IP data."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tda-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: MT-Data-Answer
; Section: 5.6.1
; Table: 5.6.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for T6a/b errors. This is a grouped AVP, which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Two times compared: no kind says it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tda-requested-retransmission-time
; AVP: Requested-Retransmission-Time
; Command: MT-Data-Answer
; Section: 5.6.1
; Table: 5.6.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The Requested Retransmission Time shall not exceed the Maximum Retransmission Time received from the SCEF."
    text-only


;; Clause 5.7.1's tables, the CMR the MME or SGSN sends; the SCEF's (clause
;; 5.8.1) is the same print, and a rule holds in both where the SCEF's never
;; asks for a connection establishment, CONNECTION_ESTABLISHMENT (0),
;; Connection-Action's Unsigned32 value the corpus does not read.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-user-identifier-imsi
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present and shall contain the identity of the UE. This is a grouped AVP which shall contain the IMSI."
    requires User-Identifier/User-Name


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-service-selection
; AVP: Service-Selection
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present if the request is for a T6a/b connection establishment."
    present-if Connection-Action = 0


;; What the UE sent.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-extended-pco
; AVP: Extended-PCO
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present, if the MME or SGSN receives Extended PCO information from the UE."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-3gpp-charging-characteristics
; AVP: 3GPP-Charging-Characteristics
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present if the request is for a T6a/b connection establishment and may be present if the request is for a T6a/b connection update."
    present-if Connection-Action = 0


;; Held to an establishment: an update is the SCEF's request too (clause
;; 5.8.1), whose table names no such AVP.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-rat-type
; AVP: RAT-Type
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present if the request is for a T6a/b connection establishment or for a T6a/b connection update."
    present-if Connection-Action = 0


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-visited-plmn-id
; AVP: Visited-PLMN-Id
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"It shall be present if the request is for a T6a/b connection establishment or for a T6a/b connection update."
    present-if Connection-Action = 0


;; What the node has available.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-terminal-information
; AVP: Terminal-Information
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall contain the identity of the UE. It shall be present if available."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cma-5-7-1-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Connection-Management-Answer
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for T6a/b errors. This is a grouped AVP, which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Held to a success's answer, an establishment's the request's
;; Connection-Action 0.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cma-pdn-connection-charging-id
; AVP: PDN-Connection-Charging-ID
; Command: Connection-Management-Answer
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"shall be present if the answer is for a T6a/b connection establishment."
    present-if request/Connection-Action = 0 and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; What the SCEF needs to send.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cma-extended-pco
; AVP: Extended-PCO
; Command: Connection-Management-Answer
; Section: 5.7.1
; Table: 5.7.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present, if the SCEF needs to send Extended PCO information to the UE."
    text-only


;; Clause 5.7.2: the MME's configuration.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-serving-plmn-rate-control
; AVP: Serving-PLMN-Rate-Control
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.7.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"- if Serving PLMN Rate Control is configured, the MME shall include the Serving PLMN Rate Control information"
    text-only


;; Clause 5.8.1's tables, the CMR the SCEF sends.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-scef-user-identifier-imsi
; AVP: User-Identifier
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.8.1
; Table: 5.8.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present and shall contain the identity of the UE. This is a grouped AVP containing the IMSI."
    requires User-Identifier/User-Name


;; What the SCEF needs to send.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cmr-scef-extended-pco
; AVP: Extended-PCO
; Command: Connection-Management-Request
; Section: 5.8.1
; Table: 5.8.1-1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"This Information Element shall be present if the SCEF needs to send updated Extended PCO information (e.g. APN Rate Control information) to the UE."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cma-5-8-1-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Connection-Management-Answer
; Section: 5.8.1
; Table: 5.8.1-2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Experimental-Result AVP shall be used for T6a/b errors. This is a grouped AVP, which contains the 3GPP Vendor ID in the Vendor-Id AVP, and the error code in the Experimental-Result-Code AVP."
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; Clause 6.1.4, the use of sessions, in each command; the two AVPs RFC
;; 6733 defines are admitted through each body's * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [32]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rir-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Reporting-Information-Request
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ria-auth-session-state
; AVP: Auth-Session-State
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"The client (server) shall include in its requests (responses) the Auth-Session-State AVP set to the value NO_STATE_MAINTAINED (1), as described in IETF RFC 6733 [32]."
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ria-no-authorization-lifetime
; AVP: Authorization-Lifetime
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ria-no-session-timeout
; AVP: Session-Timeout
; Command: Reporting-Information-Answer
; Section: 6.1.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.2.0
"Neither the Authorization-Lifetime AVP nor the Session-Timeout AVP shall be present in requests or responses."
    absent


